From: grimtickle-overlay (local)
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: rts5453: close apply_work teardown race

Audit finding #4: the guard handler (rts5453_group_service_members) can
schedule rts->apply_work after rts5453h_remove() cancels it, because the
removing flag was set and the work cancelled outside members_lock while the
handler holds that lock across its removing check and schedule. The probe
error path also never cancelled apply_work at all.

Fix:
- Set rts->removing under members_lock in rts5453h_remove(), so a handler
  that already holds the lock either runs before the flag is set (and its
  scheduled work is then cancelled) or sees the flag and skips the member.
- Cancel apply_work (and set removing) on the err_group_leave path so a work
  queued during probe cannot outlive the devm-managed rts.
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/rts5453.c b/drivers/usb/typec/rts5453.c
index 6397eaf..6af16b9 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/rts5453.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/rts5453.c
@@ -1588,6 +1588,13 @@ static int rts5453h_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	return 0;
 
 err_group_leave:
+	/*
+	 * apply_work may already be queued (the ARA/guard paths can fire
+	 * during probe); cancel it before the devm-managed rts is torn down
+	 * so it cannot run on freed memory.
+	 */
+	WRITE_ONCE(rts->removing, true);
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&rts->apply_work);
 	rts5453_group_leave(rts);
 err_unregister_ports:
 	/*
@@ -1603,8 +1610,22 @@ static int rts5453h_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 static void rts5453h_remove(struct i2c_client *client)
 {
 	struct rts5453h *rts = i2c_get_clientdata(client);
+	struct rts5453_irq_group *group = rts->irq_group;
 
+	/*
+	 * Set the removing flag under members_lock so a concurrently-running
+	 * guard handler (which holds members_lock across its removing check
+	 * and apply_work schedule) cannot pass the check and re-queue
+	 * apply_work after the cancel below. Otherwise the handler could
+	 * schedule apply_work between the flag write and the cancel, and it
+	 * would then run on freed memory after remove() returns.
+	 */
+	if (group)
+		mutex_lock(&group->members_lock);
 	WRITE_ONCE(rts->removing, true);
+	if (group)
+		mutex_unlock(&group->members_lock);
+
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&rts->apply_work);
 
 	device_remove_file(&client->dev, &dev_attr_disable_pd_interrupt);
